Module quittance "Quittance" {
  Description "Links outward from the Arch: a ship left in the Slack, and a ship given a quay.".

  // ── World events, read: the Honest Bell and the Roll ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Observe lore_bell_ship at arch_hall when befell(remainder_harboured) and not befell(remainder_kept) "Mr Prest has a new column in the Roll, ruled that morning, headed ARRIVALS WITHOUT AN ARCH. There are forty-odd entries in it, in forty hands, none of them his. 'They came ashore,' he says, 'in the south, off a ship. A town found them a quay. They declared nothing. The Bell was not asked.' He looks at the Bell. 'I have never wished so much that it had been.'".
  Observe lore_bell_kept at arch_hall when befell(remainder_kept) "The Honest Bell has been wrapped, overnight, in a cloth that was not there at close. Mr Prest says he did not do it. 'A ship that was not harboured,' he says. 'Left. With her people. It has made the Bell shy.' He lifts the cloth and lets it drop. 'It does not like to hear of a declaration that nobody was there to make.'".

  // ── A road with no duty paid, and a debt of fourteen days ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Quittance reckons in what is owed. Two things that were settled in the west and kept no receipt come in as
  // entries Mr Prest does not know where to enter.
  Observe lore_prest_road at arch_hall when befell(calx_opened) "Mr Prest has ruled a new column in the Roll in red, headed ROADS WITH NO DUTY. There is one entry in it, in his own hand, and it is two miles long: the Aenean pavement under a ridge in the west, opened, they say, by strangers with a pot of lamp oil. 'Nobody has levied on it,' he says. 'I have looked. There is a toll-house on the hill and it faces the wrong way.' He taps the column. 'It is the first road I have ever wished were mine.'".
  Observe lore_prest_names at arch_hall when befell(tallow_names) "Mr Prest has found, folded into the back of the Roll where a debt would be, a sheet in a stranger's pencil: fourteen names, and against each a day's wage, and the word PAID in a different ink for each. 'Sixty years late,' he says, 'by a village.' He smooths it. 'The Office would say it is out of time. The Bell has not said anything.' The Honest Bell, over his head, does not.".
}
